* ''Kahua lifts stay warded'' (operator, after the four-scale talk-story). At every scale the reach law holds: the working top serves as the free local floor the AI writes on, and a lift crosses devices, since the stage syncs to every device the face wears, so it takes the face's own hand, one passphrase per verified batch (`L21`), never an operator's or a temple's. Memory steers the spirit (the Lares read the kahua at cold boot), so it carries weight the way code does. Civic and shared stages compose several warded hands by threshold, and each plane's count rests on its own civic ruling (unbuilt). The ward travels with the face across temples with no registry. The batch lift serves as the household's feeding rite, its cadence wholly the person's own, with no timer and no nudge. This amends the 2026-11-04 line that named every lift free; the `lift.capability-tension` loop closes for the daemon and kahua wikis with the ward (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture#/faces-fleets-and-the-ward`>>).

